The Home Screen interface is vertically structured from top to bottom, comprising the status bar, widgets, an application icon grid, a page search utility, and the dock.
•	Status Bar: Spanning the uppermost portion of the display from left to right:
o	Time: Displays the local time as 11:24. Positioned to its right is the silent mode icon.
o	Dynamic Island: The Dynamic Island is centered at the top of the display. A solid red circular indicator is visible toward its left side, consistent with the iOS screen-recording status indicator. A small orange circular indicator is visible just right of center inside the Dynamic Island, denoting that the system microphone is simultaneously active.
o	Connectivity & Power: The Airplane Mode icon denotes that wireless network transmissions are currently disabled. The adjacent battery icon appears partially filled alongside the digital percentage readout "49."
•	Below the status bar, a pair of application widgets are displayed: 
o	On the left, the Weather widget displays the text "Weather Unavailable"
o	On the right, the Calendar widget displays the text "TUESDAY 29 No events today." 
o	Below the widgets, applications are arranged across a flexible grid system, where each application icon consists of a graphic identifier paired with a text label displaying the application name.
•	Positioned just above the Dock is a persistent Search button. 
•	Pinned to the bottom of the Home Screen is the Dock—a fixed, translucent horizontal container housing four application icons.
